all right we have our share of breweries  all over the valley but now las vegas is  getting into the wine business  pine hollow winery on charleston and  rainbow is now open and as mary jane  belliesa reports the owners are serving  the community through every sip  it's a refreshing new site in fiesta  square pine hollow winery is a new small  business in the west valley opening  their doors just last month making them  the first winery to open within las  vegas city limits and the seventh winery  to open in the state owner barbara d  virgilio and her husband john moved to  las vegas from the east coast three  years ago after seeing a need for more  wineries in the area western pa where we  were from there were wineries were  popping up you know  every other corner so we decided to  bring our unique wines to the west  because  there's nothing like us here all the  wine is prepared and made in the back  room and there's a little fix for  everyone for those who have a sweet  tooth and for those looking for some  spice we have a hot pepper wine it's our  niagara vine infused with a thai chili  pepper it's not for the faint of heart i  had one customer tell me that it was an  explosion in your mouth so that's what  we go with for that one  while the pandemic did delay the opening  of pine hollow winery it didn't slow  down the production of their wine as the  owners were still able to import grapes  from the east coast bringing a little  taste of home here to las vegas  although it took more than a year to  open virgilio says their patience and  hard work has made it all worthwhile to  cater to their customers needs and the  taste of dedication is clear to see we  were determined that we would not give  up we just rolled with it reporting from  charleston and rainbow mary jane balleza  live local now
 

